ctions 3 and 4 give configurations for all the values listed in the statement, and the impossibility proof for \\(n=3,\\;k=2\\) shows that no other value can occur. Hence the answer announced in the Verdict is complete and rigorous.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\n\\begin{cases}\nk\\in\\{0,1,3\\}, & n=3,\\\\[2mm]\nk\\in\\{0,1,2,\\dots ,n\\}, & n\\ge 4 .\n\\end{cases}}\n\\]"
